      "id": "note-66ecq5z1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 740,
      "y": 850,
      "width": 2406.25,
      "height": 62.5,
      "strokeColor": "#5c5f66",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "text": "Redpanda replaces Kafka locally: same protocol and client libraries, one binary, no ZooKeeper, a fraction of the RAM.\nProduction targets real Kafka — nothing in application code knows the difference.\n\nEvery service ships traces and metrics to the collector, never straight to a backend. Swapping Jaeger for Tempo then costs one config file, not nine.",
      "originalText": "Redpanda replaces Kafka locally: same protocol and client libraries, one binary, no ZooKeeper, a fraction of the RAM.\nProduction targets real Kafka — nothing in application code knows the difference.\n\nEvery service ships traces and metrics to the collector, never straight to a backend. Swapping Jaeger for Tempo then costs one config file, not nine.",
      "fontSize": 12.5,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
